1
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:05,597
What would your first ninety days as Group Financial Controller look like?

2
00:00:06,107 --> 00:00:09,595
I run it in three phases — assess, design, institutionalise.

3
00:00:09,755 --> 00:00:14,215
Days one to thirty: map the entities, people, chart of accounts and systems;

4
00:00:14,375 --> 00:00:18,715
time the current close end-to-end; inventory reconciliations and controls.

5
00:00:19,225 --> 00:00:22,099
Then I publish a findings memo with quick wins —

6
00:00:22,259 --> 00:00:26,841
high-risk reconciliations, cut-off fixes, ERP functionality we already own.

7
00:00:27,351 --> 00:00:32,204
Days thirty-one to sixty: a redesigned close calendar with hour-level ownership;

8
00:00:32,364 --> 00:00:39,223
a consolidation pack and eliminations matrix; a controls matrix for segregation of duties and delegation limits;

9
00:00:39,383 --> 00:00:44,111
and policy papers for the highest-risk areas — revenue, leases, credit losses.

10
00:00:44,621 --> 00:00:49,852
Days sixty-one to ninety: run one full close under the new framework and measure it —

11
00:00:50,012 --> 00:00:53,404
close days, reconciliation completion, late adjustments.

12
00:00:53,564 --> 00:00:57,781
Publish the KPIs and deliver the first board-standard reporting pack.

13
00:00:58,291 --> 00:01:03,493
Success looks like: a faster close, key reconciliations one hundred per cent current,

14
00:01:03,653 --> 00:01:07,467
and a leadership team that trusts the numbers without a caveat.
